\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{(a)}\quad &2\mathrm{HNO_3} + \mathrm{Ca(OH)_2} \rightarrow \mathrm{Ca(NO_3)_2} + 2\mathrm{H_2O}\\[4pt]
\text{(b)}\quad &2\mathrm{NaOH} + \mathrm{H_2SO_4} \rightarrow \mathrm{Na_2SO_4} + 2\mathrm{H_2O}\\[4pt]
\text{(c)}\quad &\mathrm{NaCl} + \mathrm{AgNO_3} \rightarrow \mathrm{AgCl} + \mathrm{NaNO_3}\\[4pt]
\text{(d)}\quad &\mathrm{BaCl_2} + \mathrm{H_2SO_4} \rightarrow \mathrm{BaSO_4} + 2\mathrm{HCl}
\end{aligned}
\]

Thus, the balanced chemical equations are as given above.
